Psalm 119:33-40

33 LÓRD, téach me the wáy of your státutes,
and I will kéep them to the énd.
34 Gránt me ínsight that I may kéep your láw,
and obsérve it wholehéartedly.

35 Guíde me in the páth of your commánds,
for in thém is my delíght.
36 Bénd my héart to your decrées,
and not to wróngful gáin.

37 Túrn my éyes from gázing on vánities;
in your wáy, give me lífe.
38 Fulfíll your prómise to your sérvant,
that yóu may be revéred.

39 Túrn awáy the táunts I dréad,
for your decrées are góod.
40  Sée, I lóng for your précepts;
give me lífe by your jústice.

Glóry to the Fáther, and to the Són,
and to the Hóly Spírit:
as it wás in the begínning, is nów,
and will be for éver. Amén.
